<%# THE EXITS LAB'S OWN FEW RULES, on top of `lab/_styles` and the `debug`
    layout's, and in their palette -- NO NEW COLOURS. Every value below is
    already in `app/views/layouts/debug.html.erb` or
    `app/views/lab/_styles.html.erb`.

    THERE ARE THREE, and each is here because this lab has a shape the first one
    does not: a block per NAMED PLACE rather than a table of rooms, since every
    place in an exits answer is separately judged and separately expected. %>
<style>
  /* ONE PLACE THE ANSWER NAMED. A bordered block rather than a table row,
     because it carries a teaser, four picks, what the engine did with them and
     his verdict -- which is more than a row wraps usefully. */
  .place { border: 1px solid #21262c; padding: .5rem .7rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }

  /* THE ONE WHOSE PICK REACHED THE WORLD gets the accent the debug view gives
     the current turn, because it is the only kind of pick that decided
     anything. */
  .place.reaching { border-color: #4a4326; background: #14140f; }

  /* AND A PLACE HE TYPED THAT NO DRAW HAS NAMED. Dimmer than a drawn one and
     never coloured as a miss: an unnamed expectation is out of the denominator,
     not a failure. `Lab::Exits::Judgement`'s header has the measurement behind
     that rule. */
  .place.unmet { border-style: dashed; }
</style>
